SECRETS

- (secrets) gives an alist of (key . description) ; values hidden.
- (secret "REPL_TOKEN") gives value as tainted string. Acts like a string in all
  string functions; taint propagates through result. Prints redacted as a
  hash-and-angle-brackets printout naming only the key. Revealed only when
  serialized into outgoing MCP call argument or header.
  Only REPL_-prefixed keys are visible.
  Example: (load-mcp :name "acme" :url "…" :headers (list (cons "Authorization" (secret "REPL_ACME_TOKEN")))) .

String built-ins are taint-aware: taint flows through every result computed
from a secret.

GOTCHAS

- Secret printout cannot be read back. Typing one into a form is always an
  error. Call (secret "KEY") again, or use the name you bound it to.
